# New branch required

Do not implement or commit features, bugfixes, or other product changes on `master`.
Documentation-only and build-system changes may stay on the current branch.

Before making a change that needs a branch, check whether the current branch already
is the requested work.

- If it is, continue on that branch.
- Otherwise, create a new branch from current `master` first (`feat/…` or `fix/…`), then make
  changes there.
- Before creating or switching to that branch, check for uncommitted changes. If the worktree
  is dirty, stop and ask the user what to do; do not switch or stash. Proceed only when it is
  clean.
- Do not merge or push to `master` unless the user explicitly asks.

Documentation includes README, changelog, and other markdown that does not change behavior.
Build-system changes include CI workflows, Dependabot, and project or SDK configuration that
does not change library behavior.
